### What's allowed (noncommercial use)

You may **use, run, self-host, modify, study, and redistribute**
NimbusGuard (and any of its forks or derivative works) for:

- Personal projects, research, learning, teaching, hobbies.
- Security assessments you perform on **your own** cloud
  infrastructure as part of your individual work, as long as
  you are not selling NimbusGuard or a hosted version of it
  to third parties.
- Academic and public-interest research (universities, public
  research bodies, public health / safety organizations,
  environmental protection organizations, government
  institutions).
- Internal evaluation by a commercial organization to decide
  whether to purchase a commercial license.

### What is NOT allowed without a commercial license

- Offering NimbusGuard (or a hosted, managed, or rebranded
  version of it) as a **paid service** to customers.
- Using NimbusGuard inside a **commercial product or paid
  SaaS** as a core differentiator.
- **Selling** NimbusGuard, its derivatives, or access to any
  NimbusGuard-powered service.
- Using NimbusGuard to **generate revenue** directly, either
  by selling scan reports or by charging for access to a
  NimbusGuard-powered dashboard.

If you are unsure whether your use is permitted, or if you
want a commercial license, please contact the licensor at
the GitHub repository at
<https://github.com/cerez23/nimbusguard>.

